{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":852384,"items":[{"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n        <jats:p>Lot of research work has been done regarding the classical theorem known as Enestr\u00f6m-Kakeya theorem concerning the regions containing zeros of a polynomial. This theorem states that if <jats:italic>F(z)<\/jats:italic> = \u2211<jats:sup><jats:italic>n<\/jats:italic><\/jats:sup><jats:italic> <\/jats:italic><jats:sub><jats:italic>\u03bb=0<\/jats:italic><\/jats:sub><jats:italic> f<\/jats:italic><jats:sub><jats:italic>\u03bb<\/jats:italic><\/jats:sub><jats:italic>z<\/jats:italic><jats:sup><jats:italic>\u03bb<\/jats:italic><\/jats:sup> is a polynomial with degree n with real coefficients satisfying 0 \u2264 <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>0<\/jats:sub> \u2264 <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>1<\/jats:sub> \u2264 <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>2<\/jats:sub> \u2264 \u00b7 \u00b7 \u00b7 \u2264 <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>n<\/jats:sub>, then all the zeros of <jats:italic>F<\/jats:italic>(<jats:italic>z<\/jats:italic>) lie in |<jats:italic>z<\/jats:italic>| \u2264 1. In this article, we prove several extensions of this theorem which impose restrictions only on the coefficients <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>0<\/jats:sub>, <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>1<\/jats:sub>, \u00b7 \u00b7 \u00b7 , <jats:italic>f<\/jats:italic><jats:sub>n\u22121<\/jats:sub> and leaves the coefficient fn to vary freely over the whole complex plane.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.21203\/rs.3.rs-3187753\/v1","type":"posted-content","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["On the zeros of polynomial with real coefficients"],"author":[{"given":"Mohammad Ibrahim Mir","family":"Ibrahim","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Kashmir"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Jamina Banoo","family":"Jamina","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Kashmir"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,7,26]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.21203\/rs.3.rs-3187753\/v1"},{"DOI":"10.4064\/aa8647-11-2017","title":["Real zeros of the Hurwitz zeta function"],"author":[{"given":"Toshiki","family":"Matsusaka","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2018]]},"container-title":["Acta Arithmetica"],"type":"journal-article","is-referenced-by-count":5,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.4064\/aa8647-11-2017"},{"DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-642-05203-3_4","title":["Riemann Zeros and Factorizations of the Zeta Function"],"author":[{"given":"Andr\u00e9","family":"Voros","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2009,10,24]]},"container-title":["Lecture Notes of the Unione Matematica Italiana","Zeta Functions over Zeros of Zeta Functions"],"type":"book-chapter","is-referenced-by-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/978-3-642-05203-3_4"},{"DOI":"10.1142\/9789813230651_0018","title":["Distributions of Zeros for Zeta Functions of Reductive Groups"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2018,2,5]]},"container-title":["Zeta Functions of Reductive Groups and Their Zeros"],"type":"book-chapter","is-referenced-by-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1142\/9789813230651_0018"},{"abstract":"<jats:p>By analytically extending the Euler Zeta function, the Riemann Zeta function is obtained. The Riemann Zeta function has zero points, which are trivial and non trivial, respectively. By analyzing the internal structure of the Riemann Zeta function, it was found that the key to the value of 0 in the complex plane of the Riemann Zeta function is sin(s\u03c0)=0, thus proving the validity of the Riemann hypothesis. That is, the real parts of all non trivial zeros of the Riemannian Zeta function are on the complex plane 1\/2.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.55375\/sqpreprints.2023.4","type":"report-component","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Proof that the Real Part of All Non trivial Zeros of Riemann Zeta Functions is 1\/2"],"author":[{"given":"Xiaohui","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"container-title":["SQPreprints"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,6]]},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.55375\/sqpreprints.2023.4"},{"abstract":"<p>\n                    Let\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"chi\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>\n                            \u03c7\n                            \n                          <\/mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">\\chi<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    be a primitive, real and even Dirichlet character with conductor\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"q\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>q<\/mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">q<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    , and let\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"s\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">s<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    be a positive real number. An old result of H. Davenport is that the cycle sums\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"upper S Subscript nu Baseline left-parenthesis s comma chi right-parenthesis equals sigma-summation Underscript n equals nu q plus 1 Overscript left-parenthesis nu plus 1 right-parenthesis q minus 1 Endscripts StartFraction chi left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis Over n Superscript s Baseline EndFraction comma nu equals 0 comma 1 comma 2 comma ellipsis comma\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>S<\/mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>\n                                \u03bd\n                                \n                              <\/mml:mi>\n                            <\/mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03c7\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>=<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:munderover>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                \u2211\n                                \n                              <\/mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>=<\/mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  \u03bd\n                                  \n                                <\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>q<\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>+<\/mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                              <\/mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  \u03bd\n                                  \n                                <\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>+<\/mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>q<\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>\n                                  \u2212\n                                  \n                                <\/mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                              <\/mml:mrow>\n                            <\/mml:munderover>\n                            <mml:mfrac>\n                              <mml:mrow>\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  \u03c7\n                                  \n                                <\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                              <\/mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:msup>\n                                <mml:mi>n<\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                              <\/mml:msup>\n                            <\/mml:mfrac>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03bd\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>=<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>0<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>2<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              \u2026\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">S_\\nu (s,\\chi )=\\sum _{n=\\nu q+1}^{(\\nu +1)q-1} \\frac {\\chi (n)}{n^s}, \\nu = 0,1,2,\\dots ,<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    are all positive at\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"s equals 1 comma\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>=<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">s=1,<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    and this has the immediate important consequence of the positivity of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"upper L left-parenthesis 1 comma chi right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>L<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03c7\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">L(1,\\chi )<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    . We extend Davenport\u2019s idea to show that in fact for\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"nu greater-than-or-equal-to 1\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03bd\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              \u2265\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">\\nu \\geq 1<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    ,\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"upper S Subscript nu Baseline left-parenthesis s comma chi right-parenthesis greater-than 0\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>S<\/mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>\n                                \u03bd\n                                \n                              <\/mml:mi>\n                            <\/mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03c7\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>&gt;<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>0<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">S_\\nu (s,\\chi )&gt;0<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    for all\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"s\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">s<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    with\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"1 slash 2 less-than-or-equal-to s less-than-or-equal-to 1\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mo>\/<\/mml:mo>\n                            <\/mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>2<\/mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              \u2264\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              \u2264\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>1<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">1\/2 \\leq s \\leq 1<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    so that one can deduce the positivity of\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"upper L left-parenthesis s comma chi right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>L<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03c7\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">L(s,\\chi )<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    by the nonnegativity of a finite sum\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"sigma-summation Underscript nu equals 0 Overscript t Endscripts upper S Subscript nu Baseline left-parenthesis s comma chi right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:munderover>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                \u2211\n                                \n                              <\/mml:mo>\n                              <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                                <mml:mi>\n                                  \u03bd\n                                  \n                                <\/mml:mi>\n                                <mml:mo>=<\/mml:mo>\n                                <mml:mn>0<\/mml:mn>\n                              <\/mml:mrow>\n                              <mml:mi>t<\/mml:mi>\n                            <\/mml:munderover>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>S<\/mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>\n                                \u03bd\n                                \n                              <\/mml:mi>\n                            <\/mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03c7\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">\\sum _{\\nu =0}^t S_\\nu (s,\\chi )<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    for any\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"t greater-than-or-equal-to 0\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>t<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              \u2265\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>0<\/mml:mn>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">t \\geq 0<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    . A simple algorithm then allows us to prove numerically that\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"upper L left-parenthesis s comma chi right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>L<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03c7\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">L(s,\\chi )<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    has no positive real zero for a conductor\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"q\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>q<\/mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">q<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    up to 200,000, extending the previous record of 986 due to Rosser more than 50 years ago. We also derive various estimates explicit in\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"q\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mi>q<\/mml:mi>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">q<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    of the\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"upper S Subscript nu Baseline left-parenthesis s comma chi right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>S<\/mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>\n                                \u03bd\n                                \n                              <\/mml:mi>\n                            <\/mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03c7\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                          <\/mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">S_\\nu (s,\\chi )<\/mml:annotation>\n                        <\/mml:semantics>\n                      <\/mml:math>\n                    <\/inline-formula>\n                    as well as the shifted cycle sums\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math\/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\" alttext=\"upper T Subscript nu Baseline left-parenthesis s comma chi right-parenthesis colon equals sigma-summation Underscript n equals nu q plus left floor q slash 2 right floor plus 1 Overscript left-parenthesis nu plus 1 right-parenthesis q plus left floor q slash 2 right floor Endscripts StartFraction chi left-parenthesis n right-parenthesis Over n Superscript s Baseline EndFraction\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:msub>\n                              <mml:mi>T<\/mml:mi>\n                              <mml:mi>\n                                \u03bd\n                                \n                              <\/mml:mi>\n                            <\/mml:msub>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>s<\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>\n                              \u03c7\n                              \n                            <\/mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mo>:=<\/mml:mo>\n                            <mml:munderover>\n                              <mml:mo>\n                                \u2211\n                                \n                              <\/mml:mo>\